- Look into porting to iOS for Carplay integration
- ID3 tag editing (reading title already works, editing does not)
- CPU: add a Main-window dirty-check (like PL/EQ/Info already have) so it
  skips redraw+present when fully idle, instead of always drawing at the
  frame-cap rate. Higher-risk-than-reward: Main is by far the most stateful
  window (spectrum bar decay/peak physics, VU meters, drag state, several
  popups), so a snapshot key is more likely to miss an input and leave
  something stale on screen than it was for PL/EQ/Info - and since switching
  to GPU-accelerated rendering already cut Main's per-frame cost a lot, the
  remaining payoff is smaller than it would have been before. Not urgent.
